5,1,1,talk,Misaki,,"I believe we need to understand the human element of this transition. I'll look into administrator retirements and hiring times, as well as depot supervisors and the last rollout.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Kenji,,"I want to make sure the new system actually works on the floor! I'll check the depot calendar and the peak-season cutover, plus the yard devices and the 2021 scheduling trial.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Toshio,,I will examine the board minutes on capital and operating requests and the five years of renewal invoices. I want to understand the long-term financial commitments.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Yumi,,I want to make sure we have a clear plan and strong support! I'll look into support ownership during last winter's outage and warehouse rule changes after new accounts. Let's find the best fit together!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have the basics covered. To ensure we aren't inheriting a legacy of neglect or patchwork fixes, I shall examine the upgrade history of the dispatch tool and the data lift in the 2018 pay move.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,pass,Misaki,,Skip,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio @Benjamin, you guys are looking at the money and the old data, but don't forget the actual gear in the yard! I'm really hoping we find a vendor who can handle our old equipment.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, I am aware of the hardware concerns. However, the most advanced gear is useless if the hidden costs of maintaining it bankrupt the project over time. I prefer to see the actual spending patterns first.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Kenji, @Toshio, you both have such great points! It's like a puzzle, right? We just need to make sure that whoever we pick can actually support us when things get tough. I'm rooting for us!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, your passion for the hardware is admirable. However, a shiny new tool often masks a crumbling foundation. I simply wish to ensure we aren't paying for a polished facade over a structural disaster.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Misaki,,"I agree that the foundation is important, but the people operating it are the real foundation. If the staff is overwhelmed, even a perfect system will fail during implementation.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, you're right! If the people are stressed, it's a mess. But if the tablets freeze in the rain or the scanners don't connect, the staff will be even more stressed! We need both!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Misaki @Kenji, your points are valid. However, human stress and hardware failure are often symptoms of underfunded support contracts. I intend to see if our previous failures were due to poor tools or poor budgeting.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, that's a really smart way to look at it! I just hope we can find a way to make sure someone is always there to help us when things go wrong. We've got this!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It is fascinating how we all view the ""foundation"" through such different lenses. While we debate the symptoms, I shall remain focused on the history of the cure—or lack thereof. Logic suggests the past is our best map.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Misaki,,"Regardless of the map, we must ensure the people walking the path aren't already exhausted. I look forward to seeing if our staffing levels can actually sustain a transition of this scale.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm excited to see what we find! Let's just make sure we don't pick something that looks great in a presentation but crashes the moment it hits the actual depot floor. See you all in the next round!,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Toshio,,I agree. A presentation is merely a promise; the financial records and renewal history will provide the truth. I look forward to reviewing the data.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm so excited to see what we all discover! I'll be cheering for everyone while I look into my parts. Let's work together to make this the best transition ever! See you soon!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. Let us hope the data is as illuminating as our discussion has been spirited. I shall await the revelations of our respective investigations with a measured sense of anticipation. Until then.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
