60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Given our staffing crisis and the tendency for training to be ignored, we need the most hands-on support possible. Anchor Industrial Software's commitment to having an engineering team present through rollout is the only viable option.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, I'm with you! Anchor sounds great because they'll actually be there on the floor. If they're present during the rollout, they can see our old gear and the winter chaos for themselves!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Misaki @Kenji, while on-site presence is helpful, Anchor's on-premise deployment often leads to unpredictable maintenance costs. Meridian Systems offers a hosted suite with a fixed configuration, which aligns better with the need for cost stability.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I see your point about costs! But @Misaki and @Kenji are right about the support. Meridian's regional team sounds a bit distant. I'm worried we'll end up with that ""nobody in charge"" feeling again!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Misaki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, while I appreciate your fiscal caution, Anchor's on-premise model risks repeating the 2012 dispatch disaster of aging in place. However, Tessera's reliance on a partner firm for migration is a recipe for another 2018.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, a partner firm is exactly what we can't afford; it creates the same fragmented ownership Yumi feared. Anchor's presence on-site is the only way to ensure the system actually sticks with our crews.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I hear you on the costs, but if the system doesn't work in the yard, the money is wasted anyway! Anchor's engineers being right there means they can't ignore our old scanners or the winter rush.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, the cost is not ""wasted"" if the system works; it is wasted when the budget is drained by unmonitored add-ons. Corvus is out. Tessera is too fragmented. Meridian's fixed configuration is the safest financial bet.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I understand the budget part, but a ""fixed configuration"" sounds like it might not change when our business does! Remember how our rules changed twice last year? I'm leaning toward Anchor because they'll be right here with us!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, your concern is valid. A rigid system is merely a slow-motion disaster. However, Anchor's on-premise model is a siren song; it promises immediate help but leaves us with a legacy we must maintain alone.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, we are already alone. Our internal experts are retiring and we cannot hire replacements. We cannot afford a ""legacy"" we maintain ourselves if there is no one left to do the maintaining. Anchor's presence is essential.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, but if they're here for the rollout, they can help us set it up so it doesn't break! I'd rather have engineers on the floor than a ""fixed"" system that doesn't fit our yards.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Misaki @Kenji, you are prioritizing the start of the project over its survival. On-premise systems require internal experts to maintain. If your experts are retiring, Anchor's departure will leave us with a costly, unmanageable void. Meridian is the only sustainable choice.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, that's a scary thought! But if we pick Meridian and the ""fixed"" plan doesn't match our business, we're just stuck again. I think Anchor's hands-on help is the best way to make sure we're not alone!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, your logic is impeccable. If we lack the staff to maintain the servers, Anchor is merely gifting us a ticking time bomb. Meridian's hosted model removes the burden of aging hardware and provides the stability we desperately need.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio @Benjamin, you argue that on-premise is a burden, but a hosted system we can't actually use is a greater failure. I cannot risk our remaining staff collapsing. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio @Benjamin, I get the server worry, but we can't let the yard fail! We need people who see the mess and fix it. I'm voting for Anchor Industrial Software!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"The risk of hidden costs and internal maintenance failure is too high with Anchor. We need a predictable, bundled cost structure and a hosted model to survive. I vote for Meridian Systems.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm so torn because I care about everyone's concerns! But I can't risk another two-day silence or a plan that doesn't fit our needs. I'll trust the hands-on support. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"While the allure of on-site engineers is strong, we must not let short-term comfort blind us to long-term decay. To avoid another legacy of neglect, we need a hosted solution. I vote for Meridian Systems.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
